sections.content:
Voditelj primjećuje da je život p. Nagyja obilježio upravo Merz, toliko da se, kad netko spomene blaženika, svi sjete i njegova postulatora. Zato ga pita čime se bavi kada se ne bavi Merzom.

P. Nagy objašnjava da je paralelno radio mnogo toga:

- do nedavno je bio **profesor na isusovačkom fakultetu na Jordanovcu**, gdje je posljednjih desetak godina predavao tada najnoviji predmet, **Međureligijski dijalog**, a prije toga i mnoge druge predmete;
- nakon studija proveo je **šest godina u Rimu na Radio Vatikanu**;
- djelovao je i u **Hrvatskoj katoličkoj misiji u Parizu**.

Posebno naglašava da je usporedno radio i **pastoralno, osobito s mladima**. Upravo je mnogim mladima tako otkrio blaženog Ivana i oni su ga prihvatili. Približiti ljudima „jedan takav divan lik”, kaže, jednostavno je dužnost.

sections.content_en:
The host notes that Fr. Nagy's life has been marked precisely by Merz, so much so that when someone mentions the blessed, everyone also remembers his postulator. That is why he asks him what he does when he is not dealing with Merz.

Fr. Nagy explains that he did many things in parallel:

- until recently, he was a **professor at the Jesuit faculty at Jordanovac**, where for the last ten years or so he taught what was then the newest subject, **Interreligious Dialogue**, and before that many other subjects as well;
- after his studies, he spent **six years in Rome at Vatican Radio**;
- he also served in the **Hrvatska katolička misija u Parizu**.

He particularly emphasizes that he simultaneously worked **pastorally, especially with youth**. It was precisely in this way that he revealed Blessed Ivan to many young people, and they embraced him. Bringing "such a wonderful figure" closer to people, he says, is simply a duty.
